From f81292e132022a4b038e1f7b5f7582af30e4cbab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:17:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] port 243fdb21: serve: a request commits only the rows it
 can emit, so the parked snapshot matches what the client got (#4677)

Upstream 243fdb21 (patch and policy test by hanchengme): serve_stop_bound()
caps a verify window's accepted rows at the rows the request can still emit
(max_new - produced_n) and ends at the first EOS, before the commit, so a
request's last window no longer parks a snapshot with tokens the client never
received (conversation_prefix() refused it and the older checkpoint was used).
include/strata/core/serve_stop_bound.hpp and tests/core/serve_stop_bound_test.cpp
are upstream's unchanged; the test is registered beside conv_cache_test.

Changes against upstream:
- No #if defined(STRATA_USE_HIP) gates: it applies on CUDA too.  Upstream
  measured it only on HIP (4 x R9700); nothing in it is backend-specific.
- The pipelined loop (STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE, which STRATA_SPEC_LANES folds in)
  caps `a` before V1(A)'s commit as upstream, and that capped `a` is what the
  front stages B never ran on commit (VF(st, A).pl_commit_async(a + 1)) and
  what a launched B's undo replays (undo_keep = a + 1).  A cut window has
  a < A.T - 1, so it is never "on" and the A.T commit for the accepted-whole
  case is not reached.  Every stage holds the same rows.
- The spec lanes' own verdict (spec_lanes::verdict, the lane_verdict commit)
  already commits only the rows it emits (vd.commit); unchanged.
- Both sites cap only while produced_n < max_new: with nothing left to emit
  serve_stop_bound() returns 0 and a would be -1 (x = outp[-1]); that case
  commits as before.
- The env switch is kept as upstream: on by default, STRATA_SERVE_STOP_BOUND=0
  turns it off (the A/B against production's behaviour).

Not measured on CUDA yet.  Verified only: the engine builds; the policy test
(2,736 cases) and the CPU conversation tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
